{
  "opening": "This release introduces significant enhancements to the glom library, focusing on new specification types for data transformation and improved CLI capabilities. It also refines internal representations and public API consistency across various spec classes.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m15",
      "text": "The `glom_cli` command-line interface must accept Python-full specifications rather than being limited to AST literals, allowing for more complex logic in specs. The `mw_get_target` and `mw_handle_target` functions must correctly process targets that are AST literals or full Python expressions."
    },
    {
      "id": "m29",
      "text": "The `Auto`, `Fill`, `Iter`, and `Let` spec types must be exposed as public names within the library's main namespace. These specs enable default mode handling, streaming iteration, variable capture, and filling missing values respectively."
    },
    {
      "id": "m33",
      "text": "The `Invoke` spec type must provide a concise and readable representation when its arguments are displayed, ensuring that `repr(Invoke(...))` is shortened compared to previous versions."
    },
    {
      "id": "m34",
      "text": "The `Invoke` spec type must expose a `constants` attribute (replacing any previous `consts` name) for accessing constant values used in invocation. The internal `args` attribute of `Invoke` should no longer be considered part of the stable public API."
    },
    {
      "id": "m44",
      "text": "The `Fill` spec type must implement a meaningful `__repr__` method that clearly indicates its purpose and parameters when printed or inspected."
    },
    {
      "id": "m45",
      "text": "The `Assign` spec type and the `assign` convenience function must both have clear and descriptive `__repr__` outputs that reflect their assignment behavior."
    },
    {
      "id": "m46",
      "text": "The `Coalesce` spec type and the `Inspect` spec type must both provide reasonable string representations via `__repr__` that aid in debugging and exploration."
    },
    {
      "id": "m47",
      "text": "All public specifier types, including `Auto` and `Check`, must now have implemented `__repr__` methods that return informative strings describing the spec instance."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all named public interfaces are accessible as specified and that the CLI behaves according to the new support for Python-full specs."
}
